The case-mapping tables in packages/vm/src/values/mono-case.ts, and the same
tables in secondlife/slua's VM/src/mono_strings.cpp, which is compiled into
packages/vm/wasm/slua.wasm, derive from Mono 2.6.4's
mono/metadata/char-conversions.h. rezless distributes these tables under the
GNU Library General Public License, version 2, the licence Mono 2.6.4's
LICENSE and COPYING.LIB files give for that directory. The licence text is in
section 7 of packages/vm/wasm/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, which the @rezless/vm
package ships as wasm/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt. The tables come with no
warranty.

The Mono file has no copyright or licence notice of its own. Mono 2.6.4's
runtime sources name these copyright holders:

  Copyright 2001-2003 Ximian, Inc (http://www.ximian.com)
  Copyright 2004-2009 Novell, Inc (http://www.novell.com)

Mono removed the file in July 2015, and Mono's LICENSE file has placed its
runtime under the MIT License since March 2016. secondlife/slua publishes
mono_strings.cpp under its MIT License text. The header of mono-case.ts says
how rezless's copy differs from the original. Source code: Mono 2.6.4 at
https://github.com/mono/mono/tree/mono-2.6.4, SLua at
https://github.com/secondlife/slua, rezless at
https://github.com/i-doll/rezless.

